reply.body:
@olpaw I believe I went down this path before and that's why the code Foivos is using includes the explicit case handling for SubstitutionMethod and CustomSubstitutionMethod. There are HostedMethod instances for which getJavaMethod() is not an appropriate call.

A check that the HostedMethod implements OriginalMethodProvider would ensure that a call to getJavaMethod() returned the same result for these two cases. However, I am not sure whether that might also step sideways to the original for other cases where we might not want that to happen.

The current lookup is careful to do this same sidestep consistently for these two substitution classes to give the same view of the code base at various lookup points when feeding data to the debuginfo model (for type, method and field lookup). If we were to change this here I think we would need to change it consistently everywhere else and be sure that provides a coherent vies across the whole debuginfo model.

